   "version": 1,
   "id": "el-0337",
   "seed": 1033414373,
   "versionNonce": 745295292,
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1974.0,
   "y": 5415.630000000001,
   "width": 932.0,
   "height": 21.96,
   "strokeColor": "#1a1d23",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "Top risks and what we actually build for them",
   "originalText": "Top risks and what we actually build for them",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.22,
   "autoResize": false,
   "baseline": 14.4
  },
  {
   "isDeleted": false,
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "version": 1,
   "id": "el-0338",
   "seed": 1456822684,
   "versionNonce": 325759827,
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1974.0,
   "y": 5445.590000000001,
   "width": 932.0,
   "height": 461.5,
   "strokeColor": "#495057",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fontSize": 12.5,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "1  SEO REGRESSION ON MIGRATION \u2014 the existing URLs are the asset, and a\n   rebuild is the single most common way to lose organic traffic.\n   Build: crawl and freeze the current URL inventory, redirect table\n   loaded into edge KV, pre-launch diff of titles / canonicals /\n   structured data, staged traffic rollout with rank monitoring.\n\n2  SILENT LEAD LOSS \u2014 invisible and expensive.\n   Build: synthetic end-to-end lead probe every 5 min, alert on zero\n   leads in a business hour, DLQ depth alarm, weekly DB-vs-CRM reconcile.\n\n3  SPAM AND COMPETITOR PRICE SCRAPING.\n   Build: Turnstile + honeypot + per-IP buckets; dealer pricing behind an\n   authenticated scope from phase 3 rather than public HTML.\n\n4  IMAGE BLOAT FROM MARKETING UPLOADS \u2014 the usual cause of a slow site.\n   Build: the Media service enforces max dimensions, generates AVIF/WebP\n   variants, rejects anything over 8 MB, emits a blurhash placeholder.\n\n5  SINGLE-WRITER POSTGRES IS A SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE.\n   Build: multi-AZ with automatic failover, PgBouncer reconnect, and a\n   read-only degraded mode so the catalogue keeps serving from cache\n   even while the primary is being replaced.\n\n6  VENDOR CONCENTRATION (one PaaS + one CDN).\n   Build: ship as a container and keep the DB plain Postgres, so leaving\n   is a weekend of work rather than a rewrite.",
   "originalText": "1  SEO REGRESSION ON MIGRATION \u2014 the existing URLs are the asset, and a\n   rebuild is the single most common way to lose organic traffic.\n   Build: crawl and freeze the current URL inventory, redirect table\n   loaded into edge KV, pre-launch diff of titles / canonicals /\n   structured data, staged traffic rollout with rank monitoring.\n\n2  SILENT LEAD LOSS \u2014 invisible and expensive.\n   Build: synthetic end-to-end lead probe every 5 min, alert on zero\n   leads in a business hour, DLQ depth alarm, weekly DB-vs-CRM reconcile.\n\n3  SPAM AND COMPETITOR PRICE SCRAPING.\n   Build: Turnstile + honeypot + per-IP buckets; dealer pricing behind an\n   authenticated scope from phase 3 rather than public HTML.\n\n4  IMAGE BLOAT FROM MARKETING UPLOADS \u2014 the usual cause of a slow site.\n   Build: the Media service enforces max dimensions, generates AVIF/WebP\n   variants, rejects anything over 8 MB, emits a blurhash placeholder.\n\n5  SINGLE-WRITER POSTGRES IS A SINGLE POINT OF FAILURE.\n   Build: multi-AZ with automatic failover, PgBouncer reconnect, and a\n   read-only degraded mode so the catalogue keeps serving from cache\n   even while the primary is being replaced.\n\n6  VENDOR CONCENTRATION (one PaaS + one CDN).\n   Build: ship as a container and keep the DB plain Postgres, so leaving\n   is a weekend of work rather than a rewrite.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.42,
   "autoResize": false,
   "baseline": 10.0
  },
  {
   "isDeleted": false,
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "version": 1,
   "id": "el-0339",
   "seed": 1902607235,
   "versionNonce": 1058676934,
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 5971.090000000001,
   "width": 2920,
   "height": 18.2,
   "strokeColor": "#6c757d",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "text": "Legend:  green = system of record / recommended choice   \u00b7   red = rejected option   \u00b7   amber = viable alternative or partial adoption   \u00b7   [seam] = the service boundary to extract first when phase 3 arrives   \u00b7   dashed container = logical grouping, not a deployment unit.",
